===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*deḱ-}}
From the following:<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=4778684563|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref>

* {{der|en|la|decōrus|t=becoming, fitting, proper, suitable}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ous|pos={{glossary|suffix}} {{glossary|adjective}}s denoting presence of a quality in any degree, typically an abundance}}. {{m|la||Decōrus}} is derived from {{m|la|decor|t=elegrance, grace; charm beauty}} + {{la|en|-us|pos=suffix forming adjectives}}; and {{m|la||decor}} is from {{m|la|decēre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|decet|t=to adorn; to be decent; to be proper or suitable}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*deḱ-|t=to perceive; to take}}.
* Possibly also influenced by {{der|en|LL.|decorōsus|t=beautiful; elegant}}, from {{m|la|decoris}} + {{m|la|-ōsus|pos=suffix meaning ‘full of’ forming adjectives from {{glossary|noun}}s}}. {{m|la||Decoris}} is the {{glossary|genitive}} {{glossary|singular}} of {{m|en|decus|t=beauty, grace, ornament, splendour; distinction, glory, honour}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*déḱos|t=that which is proper}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*deḱ-}} (see above).

