===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[mark#Verb|Marked]] by [[behavior|behaviour]], [[manners]], etc., [[regard#Verb|regarded]] as [[proper#Adjective|proper]], [[tasteful]], and in [[accordance]] with [[accepted#Adjective|accepted]] [[standard#Noun|standards]].
#: {{antonyms|en|indecorous|undecorous}}
#* {{RQ:Wollstonecraft Vindication Women|edition=US|section=III|page=174|passage=The narrow path of truth and virtue inclines neither to the right nor left—it is a ſtraightforward buſineſs, and they who are earneſtly purſuing their road, may bound over many '''decorous''' prejudices, without leaving modeſty behind.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Vanity Fair|LXI|passage=There came a day when the round of '''decorous''' pleasures and solemn gaieties in which Mr. Jos Sedley’s family indulged was interrupted by an event which happens in most houses.}}
#* {{RQ:Maugham Moon and Sixpence|chapter=XLIII|passage=But who can fathom the subtleties of the human heart? Certainly not those who expect from it only '''decorous''' sentiments and normal emotions.}}
#* {{RQ:Mitchell Gone with the Wind|chapter=I|passage=The green eyes in the carefully sweet face were turbulent, willful, lusty with life, distinctly at variance with her '''decorous''' demeanor.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[appropriate#Adjective|Appropriate]], [[suitable]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:suitable}}
#: {{antonyms|en|Thesaurus:unsuitable}}

